      "limitation": "The source-feasibility screen evaluates eight plausible public sources against seven locked gates. None combines data-centre specificity, realized construction activity, project or regional linkage, quarterly frequency, public retrieval and revision provenance. The Alberta announcement ledger adds 22 AI-relevant publisher records, including four under-construction stage candidates, but zero verified realized onset or dose records. The implemented Edmonton screen identifies 17 explicit data-centre permit candidates from 85 broad records, but finds no explicit AI references and no candidate occupancy dates. The Statistics Canada capex screen adds 294 annual Canada/province cells for NAICS 51 construction capital from 2006-2026, but the industry is broad and the series is annual. The 2024 commercial-building energy survey collects data-centre operating characteristics, yet public results do not expose building-level construction dose. Announcements, publisher stages, permit values, operating stock, broad-sector capex, employment and large-load connection states remain non-authorizing proxies."
